\paragraph{Quality control.} Before the main runs, stratified samples of 100 questions were reviewed against the rendered filing. The review was performed by an AI assistant under the author's direction. Rounds one to three scored 87, 76 and 96 of 100, failing on question wording; the builder was revised after each. Round four scored 98 of 100, meeting the protocol's threshold of 98, and the dataset was frozen with a SHA-256 fingerprint (\texttt{<< d.frozen.fingerprint[:16] >>\ldots}). All 400 reviewed gold values were judged correct. The author did not independently verify the full sample (Section~\ref{sec:limits}).

\paragraph{Checker and metrics.} Models return JSON with a value, scale, page and quoted line, or \texttt{not\_found}. An answer passes when it parses, cites a page that was shown, quotes text verbatim from that page, and the value appears in the quote (Figure~\ref{fig:checker}). The prompt asks for the complete line, but the checker accepts any contiguous passage after normalising whitespace: << d.robustness.correct_partial_quote|thou >> of the << d.robustness.correct|thou >> correct plain-setup answers across the ten models quote something other than one whole line. Sign is not graded because filers display negative values inconsistently. \emph{Accuracy} is the share of the 875 answerable questions answered correctly with passing evidence. The \emph{confident-wrong rate} is the share of all 1,000 answers that give a wrong value for an answerable question and pass every check. Answers that invent a figure on S8 are counted separately, as failed abstentions. \emph{Abstention accuracy} is the share of S8 questions answered ``not found''. Rates carry 95\% Wilson intervals \citep{wilson1927}. Paired comparisons use exact McNemar tests \citep{mcnemar1947} with Holm correction \citep{holm1979} at $\alpha=0.05$. For each metric, the << d.setup_tests|length >> within-model setup comparisons form one family (Appendix~\ref{app:within}), and the pairwise model comparisons within each setup form another.

